## Replay testing

Build replay tests from stored DailySummary and Date.md records. A replay must produce the same validation/fallback/order-intent result.

## Determinism

- Use fixed timestamps in tests.
- Mock market calendars.
- Mock LLM responses.
- Do not call external APIs in unit tests.

## Assertions

Prefer explicit invariant assertions:

```python
assert sum(target_weights.values()) == 100
assert 10 <= cash_target_percent <= 30
assert 15 <= gold_target <= 25
assert config.trading.mode == TradingMode.PAPER
assert order_intent.mode == "paper"
```


## DecisionSnapshot and replay tests

Every trading decision must be reproducible. Persist a DecisionSnapshot containing:

- decision_id
- timestamp
- market
- input_snapshot_hash
- date_ids_used
- llm_raw_output_path
- parsed_decision
- validation_result
- risk_filter_result
- order_intent
- paper_fill
- portfolio_before
- portfolio_after

Required replay invariant:

```text
same Date.md
same DailySummary
same LLM raw output
same portfolio snapshot
→ same validation_result
→ same order_intent
```

Do not implement analysis → broker.buy() direct flows. The pipeline must be:

```text
LLM Decision → ParsedDecision → ValidationResult → RiskApprovedDecision → OrderIntent → PaperBroker.fill()
```


## PaperBroker is the long-term paper source of truth

Use the internal PaperBroker ledger for long-horizon paper trading. KIS mock/virtual adapters are excluded from the MVP default path.

Required PaperBroker invariants:

```text
OrderIntent accepted → paper_order recorded
paper_order filled → paper_fill recorded
paper_fill recorded → position and cash ledger updated
position/cash updated → nav snapshot reproducible
same snapshot + same order → same fill result
```

KIS account/API key changes must not reset internal paper performance history.

## Adapter test boundaries

- Unit tests must mock all external APIs.
- PaperBroker tests must not call KIS.
- KIS live tests must be read-only unless the user explicitly enables tiny-live smoke testing.
- Tiny-live order tests must be manual, capped, and never LLM-triggered.

Add golden fixtures for:

- simple KR BUY paper fill
- simple KR SELL paper fill
- simple US BUY paper fill
- paper NAV snapshot after fill
- paper MDD calculation across ISA + regular account roles
- KIS API key/account replacement recorded as Debug event
